---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';

const headings = [
  { id: 'crates', text: 'Crates', level: 2 },
  { id: 'pipeline', text: 'Pipeline', level: 2 },
  { id: 'parsing', text: 'Parsing', level: 2 },
];
---

<DocsLayout title="Architecture" headings={headings}>
  <p>MarkRust is a Rust workspace with a GUI-agnostic core and a GPUI application shell.</p>

  <h2 id="crates">Crates</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={`markrust-core     Buffer, parser, undo, spans\nmarkrust-editor   Layout, masking, GPUI element\nmarkrust-app      Window, workspace, file tree\nmarkrust          Binary entry point + CLI`} lang="text" />

  <h2 id="pipeline">Pipeline</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>User input modifies a <code>ropey</code> text buffer</li>
    <li>A background task parses Markdown with <code>comrak</code> and produces revision-stamped source spans</li>
    <li><code>RichEngine</code> derives a <code>RichTree</code> for WYSIWYG rendering and edit commands</li>
    <li>Source mode computes delimiter visibility; WYSIWYG renders the rich tree directly</li>
    <li>GPUI paints the resulting styled blocks and glyph runs each frame</li>
  </ol>

  <h2 id="parsing">Parsing</h2>
  <p>Comrak is the shared Markdown grammar for source spans, the WYSIWYG tree, and HTML export. Tree-sitter is used only to highlight supported fenced-code languages.</p>
  <p>See the repository’s <a href="https://github.com/alexey-a-abramov/markrust/blob/main/docs/architecture.md">architecture reference</a> for detailed design notes.</p>
</DocsLayout>
